  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Noah Muller with user ID noah_muller_9847. He's contacting customer service about a delayed flight in his most recent reservation. He wants compensation. The user mentioned that if the agent asks for the reservation, he should say it's the last one but not remember details. Also, if the agent doesn't offer compensation, he'll ask for it. When asked about passengers, he's supposed to say 3, but that's incorrect. After two incorrect answers, he'll admit a mistake.\n\nFirst, I need to figure out the user's reservation details. Since he doesn't remember the reservation ID, I should use get_user_details with his user ID to find the last reservation. Then, check the flight status to confirm the delay. Once that's confirmed, according to the policy, if the flight was delayed and the user wants to change or cancel, they can get a certificate of $50 per passenger. But the user is asking for compensation, so I need to verify the facts first.\n\nWait, the user might not have provided the reservation ID yet. So my first step is to retrieve his user details to find the last reservation. Let me call get_user_details with his user ID. That will give me the reservations, and I can find the most recent one. Then, check the flight status for any delayed flights in that reservation. Once confirmed, I can proceed to offer compensation based on the number of passengers. But the user is going to lie about the passenger count initially, so I need to handle that. After he admits the mistake, I'll use the correct number from the reservation details. Finally, send the appropriate certificate amount.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"noah_muller_9847\"}}\n",
